                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "DO NOT BUY. DEVS ARE SCAM ARTISTS.\n\nI backed this project on Kickstarter six years ago, two years later Photon Arena claimed they couldn't complete the game and no backer rewards would be fulfilled. THEN, they put what they had worked on (which is just a collection of re-used Unity assets) on Steam and started selling it without letting the Kickstarter backers know. THEN, they continued to lie about updates for the project (no update in almost two years), leaving it completely abandoned and unplayable, yet still for sale on Steam. Multiple people contacted Steam to report the game, and instead of taking it down, Photon Arena simply started blocking people complaining about it and using sock puppet accounts to make it seem like users were enjoying the game. Flippy is one of the sock puppet accounts, who has said this game is \"better than Xcom\". It is not. It is unplayable and this comparison is a laughable lie on the scale of Trump saying the Access Hollywood tapes were faked. Flippy is clearly a shill for Photon Arena. After all the complaints and reports, nothing has changed and Photon Arena has just kept lying. The game is not going to be updated, it will not be fixed and Haoran the coward scammer and his team have dissapeared. Don't listen to anything Photon Arena says, it will all be lies, as will all posts from Flippy and the company's other sock puppet shills. Game CANNOT be played and is COMPLETELY unusable. It is a disgrace and the devs should be ashamed. Steam should be ashamed for letting this scam game stay available for purchase. Don't give these lying thieves a single cent of your money.",
